{"content":[{"c":["MISCARRIAGE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Spontaneous abortion of a nonviable fetus. It occurs in both human (",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.16","r":"Job.3.16","rawR":"Job.3.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.16","value":"Job.3.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 3:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.9.14","r":"Hos.9.14","rawR":"Hos.9.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.9.14","value":"Hos.9.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 9:14"},") and animal (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.31.38","r":"Gen.31.38","rawR":"Gen.31.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.31.38","value":"Gen.31.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 31:38"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.21.10","r":"Job.21.10","rawR":"Job.21.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.21.10","value":"Job.21.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 21:10"},") pregnancies. The major problem is not in being unable to conceive or to become pregnant but in carrying the pregnancy to full term. The curse of a “miscarrying womb” results in not being able to have children (",{"href":"?bref=Hos.9.14","r":"Hos.9.14","rawR":"Hos.9.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.9.14","value":"Hos.9.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 9:14"},"), while the blessing of God results in successful pregnancies and long life (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.23.26","r":"Exod.23.26","rawR":"Exod.23.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.23.26","value":"Exod.23.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 23:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The time factor is the key abnormality as indicated by premature delivery or “untimely birth” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.58.8","r":"Ps.58.8","rawR":"Ps.58.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.58.8","value":"Ps.58.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 58:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.16","r":"Job.3.16","rawR":"Job.3.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.16","value":"Job.3.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 3:16"},"). While miscarriages occur for many reasons, Scripture mentions two: improper care (in animals) (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.31.38","r":"Gen.31.38","rawR":"Gen.31.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.31.38","value":"Gen.31.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 31:38"},") and trauma to a pregnant woman (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.21.22","r":"Exod.21.22","rawR":"Exod.21.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.21.22","value":"Exod.21.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 21:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.5.1-31","r":"Num.5.1-31","rawR":"Num.5.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.5.1-31","value":"Num.5.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 5"}," gives the test for an unfaithful wife. If she is guilty of adultery, then “her abdomen will swell and her thigh waste away” (v ",{"href":"?bref=Num.5.27","r":"Num.5.27","rawR":"Num.5.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.5.27","value":"Num.5.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"27"},", ",{"c":["niv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). These phrases may be euphemisms for miscarriage or for sterility (see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Paul underscores his inherent unworthiness to be an apostle by comparing his spiritual birth to an untimely physical birth (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.8","r":"1Cor.15.8","rawR":"1Cor.15.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.8","value":"1Cor.15.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Barrenness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Barrenness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Barrenness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Barrenness"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Miscarriage","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jb 3:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.3.16","rawQueryValue":"Job.3.16","sourceRefExact":"Job.3.16"},{"anchorText":"Hos 9:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.9.14","rawQueryValue":"Hos.9.14","sourceRefExact":"Hos.9.14"},{"anchorText":"Gn 31:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.31.38","rawQueryValue":"Gen.31.38","sourceRefExact":"Gen.31.38"},{"anchorText":"Jb 21:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.21.10","rawQueryValue":"Job.21.10","sourceRefExact":"Job.21.10"},{"anchorText":"Hos 9:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.9.14","rawQueryValue":"Hos.9.14","sourceRefExact":"Hos.9.14"},{"anchorText":"Ex 23:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.23.26","rawQueryValue":"Exod.23.26","sourceRefExact":"Exod.23.26"},{"anchorText":"Ps 58:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.58.8","rawQueryValue":"Ps.58.8","sourceRefExact":"Ps.58.8"},{"anchorText":"Jb 3:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.3.16","rawQueryValue":"Job.3.16","sourceRefExact":"Job.3.16"},{"anchorText":"Gn 31:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.31.38","rawQueryValue":"Gen.31.38","sourceRefExact":"Gen.31.38"},{"anchorText":"Ex 21:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.21.22","rawQueryValue":"Exod.21.22","sourceRefExact":"Exod.21.22"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.5.1-31","rawQueryValue":"Num.5.1-31","sourceRefExact":"Num.5.1-31"},{"anchorText":"27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.5.27","rawQueryValue":"Num.5.27","sourceRefExact":"Num.5.27"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 15:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.15.8","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.15.8","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.15.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9b511a11c386ff29ead0c6b2fbde300a9b3a66b432b6e19926d12553987f1e12","sourceItemName":"Miscarriage","sourceItemOrder":3